# Shop Desk — Postman collection

_Generated by StepForge — by Md Zarin Tasnim on 2026-10-07 from the **Staging** environment._

3 scenarios: Checkout with every UI step, Orders API, Data and email.

## Setup

```bash
# Postman: File → Import → shopdesk.postman_collection.json
# or the CLI: npm install -g newman
cp .env.example .env   # then fill in the values
```

## Run

```bash
newman run shopdesk.postman_collection.json --env-var adminPassword=… --env-var apiToken=…
```

## Configuration

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `BASE_URL` | Staging environment (default `https://staging.shop.test`) |
| `API_VERSION` | {{env.api-version}} (default `v2`) |
| `REGION` | {{env.region}} (default `eu`) |
| `ADMIN_PASSWORD` | secret {{secret.adminPassword}} — never commit its value |
| `API_TOKEN` | secret {{secret.apiToken}} — never commit its value |
| `DB_MAIN_URL` | "main" database (pg), e.g. postgres://user:password@localhost:5432/db |
| `DB_LOCAL_URL` | "local" database (sqlite), e.g. sqlite:./app.db |
| `DB_UNKNOWN_URL` | "unknown" database, e.g. postgres://…, mysql://… or sqlite:./app.db |
| `MAILPIT_URL` | Mailpit web/API address (default `http://127.0.0.1:8025`) |

Secret values are not part of the export: set them in `.env` locally and as CI secrets in pipelines.

## Layout

- `shopdesk.postman_collection.json` — folders per module, one sub-folder per scenario, tests per assertion

## Notes

- Captured values are saved as collection variables; objects are flattened (`{{session.token}}`).
- Exported on 2026-10-07.

